# Template for apps/autoplay-pi/.env -- this file is in git, the real .env is
# not (see .gitignore at the root of the project).
#
# Copy it and put a real secret in:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# The same string goes into the StreamAux app under Settings -> Server. The
# iCloud keychain then carries it between iPhone and iPad on its own -- but
# not retroactively to a device that happens to be offline.
#
# THE PLACEHOLDER BELOW IS DELIBERATELY TOO SHORT TO WORK. The server refuses
# to start on a key under 20 characters, and that refusal is the point: until
# 02.11.2026 the placeholder here was a 65-character sentence, which passed
# the length check and let a copied-but-unedited .env run as if it had a
# secret. In a public repository that would be worse still -- the "secret"
# would be one everybody can read. Now an unedited file stops the container,
# loudly:
#   docker compose logs autoplay-pi | tail -5
#
# Changing it later means: edit .env, docker compose up -d, and enter the new
# key in EVERY app.
AUTOPLAY_KEY=CHANGE-ME
